Important guardrail (because you said “everything anywhere”)

You can’t build this by “bypassing” protections or pulling private data.
The scalable, defensible way is:

* prioritize publicly accessible content
* use official APIs where they exist and make sense
* treat restricted platforms (LinkedIn, some review sites, Discord) as “selective ingestion”, not “total coverage”

LinkedIn is the best example: official APIs for posts/comments are restricted to approved developers. (Microsoft Learn)

You can still have strong coverage without pretending you can vacuum 100% of it.

